    {
      "id": 99,
      "type": "MarkdownNote",
      "pos": [
        1300,
        500
      ],
      "size": [
        650,
        390
      ],
      "flags": {},
      "order": 5,
      "mode": 0,
      "inputs": [],
      "outputs": [],
      "properties": {},
      "widgets_values": [
        "Official Qwen Image 2.1 Turbo INT8. Full Turbo checkpoint; no acceleration LoRA. Eight Euler steps, CFG 1. Exact sigmas: 1, 0.978453, 0.95418, 0.926626, 0.89508, 0.845148, 0.704534, 0.414568, then 0. No additional shift. Seed and ordinary user LoRAs remain available. Supply a prompt and required source/reference images. Native Qwen 2.1 VAE supports RGBA output. Base25/base40 remain available for adjustable sampling.\n\nQwen editing keeps each reference at its source dimensions (encoder resolution=0, rounded to multiples of 32). Keep the encoder latent connected to the sampler. The source controls edit dimensions, not the Create megapixel selector. The save node forces lossless PNG for further edits. Larger sources cost more memory and time. Whole-image edits still reconstruct details; use an explicit edit mask to preserve unchanged pixels.\n\nUse a different sampler seed from the image's generation seed, including between successive edits. At the same dimensions, reusing that seed can cause Qwen 2.1 noise replay (grain and halos). Seed settings remain explicit and are not silently overridden."
      ],
      "widgets_values_named": {
        "text": "Official Qwen Image 2.1 Turbo INT8. Full Turbo checkpoint; no acceleration LoRA. Eight Euler steps, CFG 1. Exact sigmas: 1, 0.978453, 0.95418, 0.926626, 0.89508, 0.845148, 0.704534, 0.414568, then 0. No additional shift. Seed and ordinary user LoRAs remain available. Supply a prompt and required source/reference images. Native Qwen 2.1 VAE supports RGBA output. Base25/base40 remain available for adjustable sampling.\n\nQwen editing keeps each reference at its source dimensions (encoder resolution=0, rounded to multiples of 32). Keep the encoder latent connected to the sampler. The source controls edit dimensions, not the Create megapixel selector. The save node forces lossless PNG for further edits. Larger sources cost more memory and time. Whole-image edits still reconstruct details; use an explicit edit mask to preserve unchanged pixels.\n\nUse a different sampler seed from the image's generation seed, including between successive edits. At the same dimensions, reusing that seed can cause Qwen 2.1 noise replay (grain and halos). Seed settings remain explicit and are not silently overridden."
      },
      "color": "#432",
      "bgcolor": "#653"
    },
